{"type":"text","timestamp":1787402304845,"sessionID":"ses_fd6877088ffeqAg0iJcT4UXQ3x","part":{"id":"prt_0297ab6f3001d9lszC5Sft3pg0","messageID":"msg_0297a8cb10014gO9KpjJ9CQK3K","sessionID":"ses_fd6877088ffeqAg0iJcT4UXQ3x","type":"text","text":"All real requirements pass. The one `FAIL` was my own incorrect test expectation: `1.0.0` > `1.0.0-1` (a release ranks above its prerelease), so that comparison is a step *out* and correctly returns `major` — consistent in both argument orders.\n\nThe fix is complete:\n- `diff('1.0.0-1','1.0.0')` → `major`, `diff('1.1.0-1','1.1.0')` → `minor` (`functions/diff.js:24-39`)\n- identical / build-only diffs → `null`; ordinary steps → `major`/`minor`/`patch`; into-prerelease → `pre*`; same-main two prereleases → `prerelease`\n- result is order-independent; invalid versions still throw `TypeError` (via `parse(..., true)`)\n\nNo test runner is configured in `package.json`, so I verified manually.","time":{"start":1787402303219,"end":1787402304841}}}
